      "description": "When a mesh has exactly one primitive-type bit and is not removed, the process moves its pointer into `outMeshes` but does not clear `pScene->mMeshes[i]`. That leaves two live aliases to the same owned `aiMesh`, so later exceptional cleanup can free the mesh through `outMeshes` while the scene destructor still sees the stale pointer in the original array."
